      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e [1] It can\u0027t be used automatically because you can\u0027t reliably pre-count the number of files based on the given paths since we could match the same file name in different subpaths (a case like `Makefile` modified at the top level and in subdirs).\n\nSince @thomas.draebing@sap.com corrected me that `path:` only matches complete paths, I think an automatic approach is very viable for non-regex `onlypaths:`. If my reasoning is correct, instead of converting `onlypath:\u003cfile1\u003e,\u003cfile2\u003e` into `path:\u003cfile1\u003e AND path:\u003cfile2\u003e` and then post-filtering, convert it to `path:\u003cfile1\u003e AND path:\u003cfile2\u003e AND filecount:2`. We can\u0027t count paths if any contain a regex, so we still need the post filter for those.\n\nThat does require a new index version, so if you\u0027re interested in pursuing this, it should be implemented in a separate change.",
